## Student flow: Homework only (don’t break)

**TEMPORARY:** Steps 2–4 are **fully removed** (code deleted). Flow is: **start → recording 1 → self-rate 1–5 → report** only. **Frontend must show the post-recording self-rate step** (e.g. "How was it? Rate 1–5") and call **POST .../self-rating** with `{ "rating": n }` before showing "Report generating" and polling for the report. To restore full flow: see `docs/TEMPORARY-REMOVED-STEPS-2-3-4-BACKUP.md` or git history.

**Single flow** under **`/v2/homework/...`**. Auth: `Authorization: Bearer <supabase_access_token>`.

**UX: Show recording right away** when the student may start. On Homework page load: (1) `GET /v2/homework/session/status`. If `has_active_session` and `session`, render current step from `session.id` / `session.status`. (2) If no active session and **`can_start_homework === true`**, call `POST /v2/homework/session/start` in the same load (e.g. useEffect) and render **task** text + record button immediately — no "Start homework" button. If **`can_start_homework === false`** (waiting for coach / `video_shown === 0` / `review_pending`), **do not** call `session/start` on load — stay on step 0 / waiting UI; `POST start` returns **409** `SESSION_START_BLOCKED`. **Step 0 coach media:** `GET session/status` returns **`tutor_video_url`** and **`tutor_video_description`** when the coach used **`POST .../send-assignment`** (optional body fields). **`assigned_exercises`** is always **`[]`** (legacy key retained for older clients).

**Endpoints:**

1. **Start** — `POST /v2/homework/session/start`, body `{}` → `{ session_id, task }` (task is a string). New sessions use DB status **`task`** (first recording step). **422** `NO_TASK_CONFIGURED` if the student has no tasks. **Task selection:** first row by `order_index` from **`tasks`** (`db.v2_get_assigned_task_for_user`). Optional score-based picker: `select_task_by_score_band()` in `v2_flow_service` (not wired). **Frontend:** Render `task`.
2. **Task (optional)** — `GET /v2/homework/session/<id>/task` → `{ task }` (string).
3. **Recording 1** — `POST /v2/homework/session/<id>/recording-1` (multipart: `audio`; optional `duration_seconds`) → `{ recording_id, task_block: { metric_question_1, metric_question_2, metric_question_3 }, recording_1_processing }`. Background job sets `performance_score_1`, `context_short`, `recording_1_performance_profile` (pace_level, filler_level), `selected_task_id`. **Focus task selection:** Per-student `v2_focus_tasks` with score band (`max_performance_score >= performance_score_1`); excludes last 5 used tasks (from `v2_student_coaching_memory.recent_focus_task_ids`); when `recurring_issues` and task `targets` exist, multi-factor scorer (`score_and_pick_focus_task`) prefers tasks matching weaknesses (e.g. too_fast → pacing, high_fillers → fillers). Tasks can have `targets` JSONB (e.g. `["pacing"]`) and `difficulty`. **Frontend:** Show metric questions; collect `answer_1`, `answer_2`, `answer_3`; POST metric-answers. **Real-time glow (optional):** During recording, send PCM16 mono chunks to **POST /v2/homework/session/<id>/recording-metrics-chunk** (binary body; headers X-Sample-Rate, X-Seq, X-T-Ms, X-Recording-Slot). Backend accepts 16k, 48k, or 44.1k (resamples to 16k internally). Pause-only: backend keeps 10 s rolling window per session; VAD 20 ms frames, pause events ≥200 ms; returns voiced_ratio, pause_score (1 = ideal). Brightness = function(pause_score). Silence-gated when voiced_ratio &lt; 0.15. Optional X-Debug for _debug (pause_ratio, pauses_per_min, max_pause_s). See **docs/REALTIME-METRICS-CONTRACT.md**. Rate limit 120/min per (user, session). Final upload still uses recording-1/recording-2 (WebM/Whisper).
4. **Metric answers** — `POST /v2/homework/session/<id>/metric-answers`, body `{ answer_1, answer_2 }` → `{ final_task }`. **Final task:** AI-generated, exactly 2 sentences: (1) "Based on [context], your task is: [focus_task]." (2) "Focus especially on [metric_answer_1] and [metric_answer_2]." 20-50 words, no extra commentary. Status → `final_task_ready`.
5. **Recording 2** — `POST /v2/homework/session/<id>/recording-2` (multipart) → `{ recording_id, performance_score_2 }`. Status → `post_questions`.
6. **Questions** — `GET /v2/homework/session/<id>/questions` → `{ questions: [ ... ] }`. **Reflective questions:** Only if admin set exactly 3 `assigned_post_question_ids` for the student. Empty or not 3 → `questions: []` (skip step).
7. **Post-answers** — `POST /v2/homework/session/<id>/post-answers`, body `{ answers: [ { question_id, answer_text } ] }` → `{ report_text, performance_score_end, performance_metrics }`. **Report (homework):** 3 paragraphs (overview, metric analysis, next steps). Status → `completed`. **Coaching memory:** Right after marking session completed, `db.v2_upsert_student_coaching_memory(user_id, session_id)` updates `v2_student_coaching_memory`: `last_5_scores`, `recent_focus_task_ids`, and `recurring_issues` (derived from last 5 sessions’ `recording_1_performance_profile`: e.g. too_fast in ≥3 of 5 → `"too_fast"`).
8. **Status** — `GET /v2/homework/session/status` → `{ session | null, session_id?, has_active_session }`. Session may include **`tutor_video_url`** and **`tutor_video_description`** (see **`docs/FRONTEND-VIDEO-AND-DESCRIPTION.md`**). There is **no countdown / tutor feedback timer anymore** on step 0. Response includes **`credits`** (integer) on both step 0 and active session — source of truth for the UI.

**Credits:** **`POST /v2/homework/session/start`** returns **402** `INSUFFICIENT_CREDITS` only if **`credits <= 0`**; any positive balance may start. **5 credits** are deducted **once** when the session **completes with a report** (balance floors at 0); **no deduction on start**. See `v2_charge_homework_completion_credits_once`, `homework_credits_charged_at`. Abandon does not charge. Frontend: show **`credits`** from **`GET session/status`**; refetch after completion. Migration: **`migrations/add_homework_credits_charged_at.sql`**.

Session statuses (possible values; flow can skip): **`task`** (first recording step; legacy rows may still show `warm_up` until `rename_homework_session_status_warm_up_to_task.sql`), `task_block`, `final_task_ready`, `post_questions`, `completing_from_recording_1`, `completed`. The student flow is **status-driven**, not a fixed 0→5 sequence: e.g. after recording-1 status may be report-generating then `completed`; step 2 can skip to report via POST complete-from-recording-1; overrides can skip step 2 or 4.

**GET report:** `GET /v2/homework/session/<id>/report` returns 200 with report payload when session is `completed`. Payload includes `report_text`, `scores`, `final_recording` (playback), `performance_history` (chart), **`report_cta`** (e.g. "Send the homework to the coach!" — show at end of report as main CTA), and optionally **`recording`** (full `transcription_text`, `filler_words_count` { total, breakdown }, `audio_url`), **`context_short`**, **`coach_insight`** (AI insight), **`admin_grade`**, and **`report_comment`**. **Frontend:** Show whole transcription, filler words used, recording playback, chart, coach_insight, and the coach-written note next to the grade when present.

