## Frontend / BFF

**Path mapping:** Frontend does **not** use `v2` in paths. It calls **`/api/admin/*`** and **`/api/homework/*`**. The Next.js BFF proxies to the backend:

- `GET/POST /api/admin/*` → `GET/POST BASE_URL/v2/admin/*`
- `GET/POST /api/homework/session/start` → `BASE_URL/v2/homework/session/start`, same for `status`, `session/:id/task`, `session/:id/recording-1`, etc.

Backend stays as-is; no change required. BFF sends `Authorization: Bearer <supabase_access_token>`.

**404 on "start" / "backend not connected"?** (1) The path must include **`session`**: correct is **`POST /v2/homework/session/start`**, not `POST /v2/homework/start`. Frontend must call **`/api/homework/session/start`** (not `/api/homework/start`). (2) Next.js must have the BFF route: without it the request hits Next.js and returns 404, so the app shows "backend not connected". Add BFF routes by copying from **`docs/homework-bff-routes/`** in this repo into the frontend app:

| Copy from (this repo) | Copy to (Next.js app) |
|----------------------|------------------------|
| `session/start/route.ts` | `src/app/api/homework/session/start/route.ts` |
| `session/status/route.ts` | `src/app/api/homework/session/status/route.ts` |
| `session/[sessionId]/task/route.ts` | `src/app/api/homework/session/[sessionId]/task/route.ts` |
| `session/[sessionId]/abandon/route.ts` | `src/app/api/homework/session/[sessionId]/abandon/route.ts` |
| … recording-1, **self-rating**, metric-answers, recording-2, questions, post-answers | … same pattern |
| `session/[sessionId]/report/route.ts` | `src/app/api/homework/session/[sessionId]/report/route.ts` |
| Optional: `session/[sessionId]/leave-report/route.ts` | Proxies **`POST /v2/homework/session/<id>/leave-report`** if the app uses the report CTA flow below |

**Report CTA (current frontend):** The main report CTA **still** calls **`POST /api/homework/session/<id>/leave-report`** (same as **`POST /v2/homework/session/<id>/leave-report`** via BFF). On **success or 404**, the client **signs out** and redirects to **`/logged-out`** with a sign-in CTA — it **does not** return the user to step 0 / **`/dashboard?homeworkState=waiting`**. No extra backend work is required for that UI change alone; if this repo’s Flask app does not register the route, the POST may 404 and the client still completes the flow.

**getAuth:** Example routes use `import { getV2AccessToken, getBackendUrl } from "../../../../getAuth"` (start/status) or `../../../../../getAuth` ([sessionId] routes). Put `getAuth` at `src/app/api/getAuth.ts` or adjust the import path. Set `NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL` or `BACKEND_URL` in frontend env.

**Reference code in this repo:** `docs/frontend-admin-panel/` (admin BFF routes, pages, components); `docs/homework-bff-routes/` (homework route .ts files). **Video + description (admin send-assignment, student homework):** `docs/FRONTEND-VIDEO-AND-DESCRIPTION.md`. Copy or adapt; ensure 401/403 and backend error bodies are handled.

**Frontend UX gotchas:** **Metric questions:** After recording-1, the backend returns `task_block.metric_question_1`, `metric_question_2`, and optionally `metric_question_3`. The frontend must render each question that has text and submit the corresponding `answer_1` / `answer_2` / `answer_3` in POST metric-answers. Show the backend error message on 422/409 so the user knows why Continue didn’t advance; show an **Abandon session** button on this step (and ideally every step). See **`docs/HOMEWORK-AND-PERFORMANCE.md`** (§3.4, §9.3).

